meta {
  name: Excuse the absence
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/attendance/periods/{{markId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "excused",
    "reason_code": "MEDICAL",
    "remarks": "Certificate seen by the class teacher."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.status: eq excused
  res.body.reason_code: eq MEDICAL
}

docs {
  Correcting one mark, as opposed to re-sending a register. The route is used
  when a certificate arrives days later and only one pupil changes.

  marked_by and marked_at are rewritten to the caller and the clock on every
  update, so the record always says who last touched it rather than who first
  took the register. The pupil, the date and the period are not editable at
  all - a mark that could move to another period would break the natural key
  it is stored under.

  This route does not re-check the school day. A class cancelled after the
  register was taken can still have its marks corrected, which is right: the
  marks are a record of what happened, and the cancellation is a statement
  about the plan.
}
